  m_Name: Tuyaux
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Fuel Injection Lines
  description: The Fuel Injection Lines are situated at the top-center-front of the
    rocket engine and are constructed from a flexible Tuyaux material, which allows
    them to navigate through the engine's compact design. These medium-sized, complex-shaped
    lines are responsible for delivering fuel to the combustion chamber, where it
    is mixed with oxidizer and ignited, producing a high-temperature and high-pressure
    gas. Interestingly, the fuel injection lines are designed to withstand the harsh
    environment of the combustion chamber, where they are exposed to extreme temperatures
    and pressures.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
